the year 2021 is nearly at a close i've  been seeing a lot of people doing recaps  of what they did or what happened to  them or  other similar things for 2021 and i  thought about that and i said well i'll  do a  video about that and i'm not going to  talk about what's coming up in 2022 i'll  probably do a separate video about that  i just thought it'd be kind of an  interesting idea to look back over  the year and there's a lot of stuff to  talk about as i went through and saw the  various things that i've done or that  i've been involved in over the last year  and some of them might be things that  you could be interested in and haven't  learned about because i'm kind of spread  out in a lot of different places so if  that's the case you can click the show  more video description below and there  will be links to all these different  things but  i'll just lead you through it right now  running through things in  you could say no particular order  although i do have them written down for  myself as notes so the first thing i  thought i would start with is i've been  now married for 10 years to andy shaka  my my wife  and we had our 10-year wedding  anniversary back in november you might  have seen that in social media  and just a few days ago we had a  different kind of anniversary so andy  and i have known each other since 1985  when she was a freshman and i was a  sophomore  in high school at catholic memorial back  in you know a long time ago and we  you know we we knew each other back then  we crossed paths again in the 90s then  we sort of you know as everybody does  lost track of each other  and we reconnected through facebook in  um  well 12 years ago  so  you know in in the very end of  2009 i'd been getting facebook  suggestions you know you should send a  friend request to this person for a  couple of months actually longer than  that and i remembered the name and i  remembered her as being somebody pretty  cool and so finally i  sent out a friend request and she  answered and that's how we actually  reconnected through facebook we started  writing each other back and forth found  we had all these common interests  eventually fell in love and then after  that after actually deciding that we  were going to get together and get  married we began talking on the phone at  a distance so there's a whole story to  be told there but you know suffice it to  say we've been together for you know a  long  time and we've also been back here in  the city of milwaukee which is not  actually where both of us grew up we  both grew up west of here andy a little  bit west me a little bit further west  out in the styx which is now  pretty developed  but we've been here in the downtown of  milwaukee uh six years we came here with  two dogs and a cat  we still uh have you know the one cat  left  sassy who is 19 years old  and you know she's also doing pretty  good this last year spent a lot of time  spending time with the sassy cat she now  sleeps most of the day downstairs in the  kids bunk bed  but you know she's pretty old so she's  doing pretty good you may have seen  pictures of me taking her outside on the  deck or other places and that's that's  us the little household now me and andy  and sassy  i've also gotten to see my oldest  daughter who lives up here  part of the time in milwaukee going to  university of wisconsin milwaukee  and you know so that that's been nice as  well  another cool thing about this year is  i've been getting in quite a bit of  regular exercise  and i have gone from  about 300 pounds down to 270 pounds  which is good you know for the  circulatory system and my knees and  everything else and that has been  through  adding a good bit of muscle and getting  rid of a lot of fat because i've been  doing the weight circuit and taking long  walks those are the majority of the  exercise i did go to a few aqua zumba  classes with andy but that wasn't really  my sort of thing so it's it's all mostly  just the weight circuit and and these  nice long walks that you may have seen  pictures from  and  what else um you know i i did academic  teaching this year  i actually taught i think  10 or 11 classes  i'll start with matc because that is in  some respects  you know i'm changing things up with  that so matc is milwaukee area technical  college which the main campus is is  about five blocks walk from here and i  finished up teaching for them i  in the  in the  spring i was teaching two classes for  them intro to philosophy online and i  was teaching in the second chance pell  program which is for  prisoners here in wisconsin i was  teaching ethics for that  and then i also taught an ethics class  in the summer and then i decided i i  don't really want to teach for matc  anymore in part because you know they  they don't pay very well and  they're kind of dysfunctional that's  that's the subject for a whole other  conversation so i just tapered off  teaching for them  i am still teaching for carthage college  which is down in kenosha but i teach  only online for them as well i i'm not  driving down to carthage and i'm not um  you know spending time on on campus  but um you know i i did teach two  classes for them  an intro to philosophy class and then a  business ethics a class that i've been  teaching for them quite a bit  and i think that's probably the last  business ethics class i'm going to teach  because things have been moving around  in the curriculum  and so now the business ethics class i'm  sort of like having to answer to two  different masters and i've decided i'm  not going to do that one anymore  instead i've been focusing a lot more on  milwaukee institute of art and design  which is the main place that i teach  every semester i teach two classes there  and then i teach a summer class so i'm  not full-time but i'm you know teaching  a pretty significant load there and  that's the cool place to teach they they  want me to teach innovative classes  and to develop them they trust me you  know a lot more you could say as a  instructor with 20 years plus of  experience  and this year it's going to be 10 years  of experience teaching online classes so  what have i taught for them well i  taught intro to philosophy in the summer  and then i also taught ethics for  artisan designers i i got to teach a new  class on ursula k le guin's earth-sea  books  i taught my philosophy mindfulness in  life which is basically a philosophy as  a way of life kind of class and then  philosophies of human nature and other  one of my staples so you know all told  looking at it i did teach in fact 10  classes this last  year  what else a lot of stuff with modern  stoicism and stoic philosophy you may  know that i  co-edited a  book that just recently came out  stoicism today selected writings volume  three it's me and leah goldrick who  edited that that was a really big  project that was funded by  a patron and the proceeds of which go to  the modern stoicism organization so  that's really cool  andy shaka and i also did something  really big this year we organized and  ran  the international stoicon conference  that was a lot of moving parts to it  and  it was it was pretty cool we did all  these things before it we've got videos  from it again you know click the links  below and you'll be taken to where you  can find all that sort of stuff i also  did some presentations at stoicon x's  i was invited to give a presentation for  stoic on x military  i did a presentation for stoicon x  norway  with andy i did a joint presentation  stoicon x uh paths to flourishing about  stoicism and marriage and there was the  marcus aurelius anniversary as well so i  did a presentation on that for the new  acropolis chicago  um i also you know i'm the editor of the  stoicism today blog  and i brought on a friend and colleague  to be the assistant editor  and that went really well and we are you  know i'm getting so much more done  having somebody to help me out  so that's that's been quite good  and i also developed a class on stoic  philosophy in addition to the epictetus  and caribbean class that i've had out  there for quite a while  i developed one for a platform called  listenable called basics of stoic  philosophy  and practice it's a really cool short  audio course  you can listen to it free if you want to  i think for seven days i'll put a link  to that below  as well  i also did some academic conferences  all of which were online nothing face to  face  i gave a paper at the saint anselm  conference which was based at saint  anselm college  in new hampshire but of course was was  online and we had an international crowd  doing that so that was really cool um  and then we we harold and i uh the guy  that i use my my assistant editor he and  i also did a presentation on pro races  in the aristotelian and stoic traditions  for the aristotle and the aristotelian  tradition conference and then both of us  actually teamed up again and did another  presentation on priorasis and epictetus  recently at the second brazilian  epictetus seminar and i should say  something about collaboration  i've got a few people that i do  collaborative work with you know i  mentioned my co-editor for stoicism  today leah and then harold is is a  somebody who i do a lot of work with i  also have a friend and colleague down in  south africa mark smith and we do some  collaborative stuff and then there's  other collaborative things that i do  that i'll get to talking about in just a  bit  i think it's worth spending some time  talking about the  youtube channel as well  not least since i'm  putting this out on youtube right  so  something really cool we passed the 100  000 subscribers mark earlier this year  on youtube and you know i've been on  youtube producing videos now for 10  years so that is  kind of cool you know to have that  footprint as they call it a digital  footprint or presence out there i think  there's a lot of people who  have benefited from these philosophy and  other videos that i do  and it's cool to see that you know  despite not putting a lot of  work into technical production and and  more just you know the thought the  content  people want that and and it's working um  we also did  a number of important videos in series  so  46 half hour hegel videos over the  course of the year  70 leguin earthsea videos and the new  speculative fiction studies  i also did some speculative fiction  studies  work on philip jose farmers the lovers  i did nine sadler's stories the most  recent of which i released just earlier  this week i remastered ten of the  epictetus and coridian videos and i have  some more of those to do i did nine  sadler's honest book reviews  i also did eight classic metal classes  with another collaborator of mine scott  tarrouli guitar professor at berkeley  school of music and a good friend and  fellow metalhead i did nine worlds of  speculative fiction videos which also  then  included live chat and  some  follow-up in video conferencing  continuing that series  you can also find videos for 20 wisdom  for life radio shows that another  collaborator of mine dan hayes and i  did this year  for riverwest radio a community radio  station here  in town and i also did um about 20 about  250  sadler's lectures and sadler shorts  podcasts  um  so that's you know some some other  presents we did a lot of cool events  amas every month  live readings from my book reason  fulfilled by revelation i shot a lot of  other kind of funny videos like the  wombo art generator ones or these  twitter conversations where somebody  like richard dawkins kind of stepped in  it captioned contests we did quite a few  of those unboxing videos and evil sadler  even showed his head so lots and lots of  video and podcast production  um what else um  i uh  i did the radio show wisdom for life but  i've also started coming on  every other week on wednesdays onto the  drive time from riverwest radio show and  that's kind of a whole different format  you know that's more  short news stories and commentary and  interviewing people and that's been a  lot of fun  so i'm really glad the station manager  asked me to after coming on for a few  interviews myself to become a regular  co-host for that  i've done a lot of podcast interviews  also some video and site interviews this  year a lot of people have been asking me  to come on their shows or you know their  podcasts and so that's been a lot of fun  as well  and then  you know a good bit of my work is  in addition to doing the public  philosophy  and the academic work and you know  stoicism today  i also have clients  and i have done a lot of work this year  with tutorials philosophical counseling  consulting academic coaching  i have been very bad about doing any  sort of marketing or promotion and  people are seeking me out instead which  is really great so i'm blessed in that  respect  and i've just been a very very busy guy  this year and i'm i'm happy that i'm  able to do this all almost all from home  which is uh  quite amazing for me and you know we're  living in a beautiful place  here in the downtown of milwaukee great  location  and so it's been a pretty good year i  would say  overall  you
 

